Article 2 (Measures by the Head of a Relevant Institution concerning Public Servants, etc. Who Have Received Improper Solicitations)
(1) The term "measures prescribed by the Supreme Court Rules" in Article 7 (4) 4 of the Act means any of the following measures:
1. Designation of a person to perform duties jointly;
2. Modification of the allocation of duties;
3. Reassignment of a case where an improper solicitation relates to a case in which litigation is pending.
(2) Before taking a measure under paragraph (1) 3, the head of the relevant institution shall hear the opinion of the relevant judicial panel.
